From 40c83ea8adf8a1c17a73116ec45e944498029584 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel JB Clark <djbclark@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 23:25:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Hardened JsonParseStrict() against non-JSON forms, quadratic
 keys and deep nesting

Under JsonParseStrict() and JsonParseFileStrict():
- Refuse unquoted object keys (JSON_PARSE_ERROR_OBJECT_BAD_SYMBOL).
- Refuse missing colons between object keys and values (JSON_PARSE_ERROR_OBJECT_COLON).
- Refuse \u0000 escapes in strings (JSON_PARSE_ERROR_STRING_NULL_ESCAPE).
- Track seen object keys in a StringSet and skip the redundant O(n)
  JsonObjectRemoveKey() scan during strict object construction, eliminating
  quadratic scaling while restoring normal replace semantics before return.
- Cap container nesting depth at 128 levels (JSON_PARSE_ERROR_MAX_DEPTH).

Lenient JsonParse(), JsonParseAll(), JsonParseWithLookup() and JsonParseFile()
keep their existing behaviour.

Changelog: Title
Ticket: none

